WEBVTT

00:03:59.378 --> 00:04:02.443
used to show the genotypes
that would result

00:04:02.443 --> 00:04:04.420
from breeding a given pairing.

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:05.465
Since then,

00:04:05.465 --> 00:04:07.781
numerous breeding initiatives
have made chickens

00:04:07.781 --> 00:04:08.947
bigger and meatier,

00:04:08.947 --> 00:04:11.556
and allowed them to lay 
more eggs than ever.

00:04:11.556 --> 00:04:12.413
Meanwhile,

00:04:12.413 --> 00:04:16.163
chicken production has shifted 
to an industrial, factory-like model,

00:04:16.163 --> 00:04:19.141
with birds raised in spaces 
with a footprint

00:04:19.141 --> 00:04:21.857
no larger than a sheet of paper.

00:04:21.857 --> 00:04:24.522
And while there’s been a shift
towards free-range farming

00:04:24.522 --> 00:04:27.324
due to animal rights 
and environmental concerns,

00:04:27.324 --> 00:04:30.606
most of the world’s more than
22 billion chickens today